From 8f8dde5242ba8e21513dd353105bc9cf5d3c0d3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work22_bt <>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 07:48:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] mm: record the allocation call stack in each heap node

Replace the single 'alloc_call_addr' field of mm_allocnode_s with a
backtrace[] array, so a heap block can be tied to the code path that
created it and not just to its immediate caller.

  backtrace[0] is the caller address the malloc API already captured and
  is written by heapinfo_update_node() exactly as alloc_call_addr was.
  backtrace[1] upwards hold the deeper frames, collected by whichever
  unwinder is configured:

    user space with CONFIG_SCHED_BACKTRACE - precise EHABI unwind through
        libgcc's _Unwind_Backtrace, no frame pointer needed. Ported from
        NuttX as lib/libc/sched/sched_backtrace.c.
    everything else - the arch up_backtrace() frame walk, which is safe in
        early-boot, IDLE and IRQ context.

The unwinder never writes backtrace[0], so a target with no unwinder keeps
exactly the caller information it has today in heapinfo, the memory leak
checker and the double-free report.

CONFIG_MM_BACKTRACE selects the depth and defaults to -1 (disabled).
CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_HEAPINFO raises the floor to 1, which is the depth the old
alloc_call_addr field represented: on a 32-bit target that keeps
SIZEOF_MM_ALLOCNODE at 16 bytes and SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE at 24, so an
existing heapinfo configuration pays no extra RAM. A deeper trace is an
explicit opt-in and costs sizeof(void *) per chunk per level.

Also exposes the recorded path through the mminfo driver:
  - HEAPINFO_DETAIL_BACKTRACE dumps the call path of every live chunk
  - MMINFOIOC_SET_BACKTRACE_SKIP adjusts the unwinder skip count at runtime
Both are driven by the heapinfo command, added in the following commit.

Also fixes the alignment search in mm_memalign(). It did pointer
arithmetic on 'struct mm_allocnode_s *' and 'struct mm_freenode_s *' where
byte arithmetic was intended, so the step advanced by
alignment * sizeof(node) and skipped all but every Nth candidate address,
and the loop bound was scaled by sizeof(node) as well. The bound is also
changed to test for room for 'size' rather than for 'alignment', which is
what the acceptance test inside the loop actually requires; expressed in
'alignment' it rejects the last candidate that would still fit whenever
alignment > size. This commit changes both SIZEOF_MM_ALLOCNODE and
SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE, which that loop scales by, so the fix belongs here
rather than separately.

CONFIG_ARCH_HAVE_BACKTRACE is introduced and selected by
ARCH_CHIP_AMEBASMART, so the arch unwinder is built where the
architecture provides it rather than being tied to CONFIG_SCHED_BACKTRACE,
which selects the libc engine and needs no arch support. mm_backtrace.c
always carries a weak up_backtrace(), so the symbol resolves on every
path the macro can take, including the kernel pass of a protected build.
